## Troubleshooting Notes

- **CDP native VLAN mismatch:** caused by different native VLANs on the two ends of a link. Fixed by using native VLAN 1 on every trunk and making the server-room uplink an access port in VLAN 200 on both sides.
- **DHCP failing (169.254.x.x):** checked SVI state, `ip helper-address`, trunk allowed VLANs, access-port VLAN, DHCP pool gateway and routing to `20.0.0.0/24`.

